### Expected behaviour

A teardown exception should not abort destruction of unrelated work queued in the same pass. `destroy_effects` (and `destroy_effect_children`) could iterate defensively — catch per item, finish the walk, rethrow at the end — so every row still gets destroyed and unsubscribed.

Related: #18414 — a render-time throw permanently leaking freshly-connected deriveds. Both are "an exception during reactive-graph maintenance leaves the graph half-linked" bugs; together they make any recurring user-code throw a session-lifetime memory leak.

